Search and rejection summary

I reviewed official Chancellery, Bundestag, BMAS, BMFSFJ, BMF/BMWK/BMWE material, plus a limited amount of parliamentary and independent follow-up material. I kept sources that added a dated Scholz-linked declaration, an enacted federal reform, or a concrete implementation structure. I rejected duplicate pages that repeated the same cabinet decision, out-of-period follow-ups that only restated 2022 commitments, and country-level context that did not establish ruler-specific conduct. A few useful pages also hit access limits or cache misses, so I relied on search snippets or alternate official pages where necessary. The main blockers remain private nuclear-policy deliberations, direct Scholz-specific police-accountability outcomes, and post-enactment service-quality measurements.

Remaining gaps

- `1B`: still missing the internal safety alternatives and command-control review behind the F-35 / nuclear-sharing choice. More search in Bundestag defense committee records or cabinet-adjacent documents would help.
- `3B`: still missing direct Scholz-specific evidence of police-accountability outcomes, especially because most policing is Länder-level. More search in BMI oversight records and federal complaint data would help.
- `5B`: still missing chancellor-level evidence on personnel selection and corrective replacement after failure outside the crisis-response bundle. More search in staffing, audit, and coordination records would help.
- `6B`: still missing post-enactment service-quality and longer-run welfare outcomes. More search in implementation evaluations and 2023 follow-up reports would help.
